Track 2: Where the Current Takes Us?
- Story & Context: On the edge of the rooftop, salt spray stinging her face, Lita whispered to no one in particular about the drowning of her old life, the metallic tang of the storm air a stark contrast to the saccharine promises of the Drowned Districts, before a sudden power surge momentarily silenced the beat, revealing only the sound of distant sirens, making her wonder if salvation lay in the chaos or just further descent into the maelstrom: "Is this the tide, or just the end of what we were?" Her confession hung in the humid air, thick with the smell of wet metal.
